WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
Two metal balls stand far apart.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.400
One is twice as wide as the other.

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.050
Put 9.0 nanocoulombs
of charge on the pair,

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.780
then join them with a long, thin wire.

5
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.040
Electrons flow along the wire.

6
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.870
Then the flow stops.

7
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.390
When it stops, which ball
holds the larger share?

8
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.420
Or do they split it equally?

9
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:25.330
In this mission, you'll see what happens
when a charged object is connected to

10
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.320
the Earth.

11
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.790
Then you'll find the one rule that decides
whether charge flows between any two

12
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.990
conductors.

13
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.840
Your mission: predict which
sphere ends up with more charge,

14
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.150
and explain why.
